00:38:05.640 --> 00:38:07.050
One more here or we go to the audience?

00:38:07.050 --> 00:38:08.727
- We have couple more.
- Okay.

00:38:08.727 --> 00:38:11.130
- Hi Gary, hi Arctic 15.
(laughs)

00:38:11.130 --> 00:38:12.507
My name's Matthew Manetta,
I'm an entrepreneur

00:38:12.507 --> 00:38:14.900
living up here in the
Nordics from the states

00:38:14.900 --> 00:38:17.170
and I have a question for you.

00:38:17.170 --> 00:38:20.320
So, what are the three
main points you look for

00:38:20.320 --> 00:38:23.373
in a project before you
devote time and money into it?

00:38:24.340 --> 00:38:26.360
- So, this has been an
interesting transition,

00:38:26.360 --> 00:38:27.560
thanks for the question.

00:38:28.780 --> 00:38:32.180
My biggest, so, early
on, I wasn't an investor.

00:38:32.180 --> 00:38:34.670
I invested in those three
very successful companies,

00:38:34.670 --> 00:38:37.840
then, I started getting
high on my own supply

00:38:37.840 --> 00:38:40.360
and thought I was special
because of those three bets

00:38:40.360 --> 00:38:42.350
and I became an investor.

00:38:42.350 --> 00:38:45.740
In hindsight, the very
obvious mistake I made is

00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:48.940
I've had a good entrepreneurial
career, I'm an operator.

00:38:48.940 --> 00:38:52.110
I'm probably even more
a COO than I am a CEO,

00:38:52.110 --> 00:38:54.850
if you really look under
the hood of how I navigate.

00:38:54.850 --> 00:38:57.910
So, the biggest mistake that I made was

00:38:57.910 --> 00:39:00.870
I would look at a business
and I believed in the thesis

00:39:00.870 --> 00:39:04.710
and I would invest in it
because I knew what I would do.

00:39:04.710 --> 00:39:06.870
But what I didn't take
into account was that

00:39:06.870 --> 00:39:10.410
the entrepreneur or the CO,
that she or he wasn't capable

00:39:10.410 --> 00:39:11.780
of doing what I would do.

00:39:11.780 --> 00:39:15.460
So, in today's world,
and I invest very rarely,

00:39:15.460 --> 00:39:17.320
'cause I think everything is
overvalued and I'm just kind of

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:20.140
waiting for the next
cycle, but once in a while.

00:39:20.140 --> 00:39:22.730
Robin Shapiro walked into
my office, she blew me away

00:39:22.730 --> 00:39:25.900
with her concept on cricket protein.

00:39:25.900 --> 00:39:29.840
So, I did some homework on it,

00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:31.870
she was unbelievably passionate,

00:39:31.870 --> 00:39:35.190
I believed in the thesis
that cricket, as a protein,

00:39:35.190 --> 00:39:37.870
as a food source, has a lot of upside.

00:39:37.870 --> 00:39:40.050
Then, I spent a lot of time asking myself,

00:39:40.050 --> 00:39:42.590
do I believe she was
in it for the long haul

00:39:42.590 --> 00:39:45.760
and could she move the
company into a totally

00:39:45.760 --> 00:39:48.110
different space if it didn't work out.

00:39:48.110 --> 00:39:51.700
I am, now, at the point, to
answer the question directly,

00:39:51.700 --> 00:39:55.440
51% of my energy is based on
do I believe in her, or him

00:39:55.440 --> 00:39:58.240
to be able to win, the jockey,

00:39:58.240 --> 00:40:00.490
49% on the horse, then away I go.

00:40:00.490 --> 00:40:03.110
I have to fall in love with the person.

00:40:03.110 --> 00:40:06.040
I prefer, at this point,
to mitigate my risk,

00:40:06.040 --> 00:40:09.990
so I'd love to invest in
somebody who has done it before,

00:40:09.990 --> 00:40:12.810
so I can look under the
hood of how they did it.

00:40:12.810 --> 00:40:15.700
And then, of course, have
to believe in the thesis.

00:40:15.700 --> 00:40:19.240
Like, no question, I can
already feel and you could see

00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:22.140
from the talk this morning that the apps

00:40:22.140 --> 00:40:24.880
that are going to be built on
top of Alexa and Google Home

00:40:24.880 --> 00:40:27.480
is going to be a place where
I do a lot of investing.

00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:32.480
And so, the jockey and the
horse, only those two variables.

00:40:32.720 --> 00:40:33.553
- [Jan] Okay.

00:40:33.553 --> 00:40:35.860
- I'm not worried about
could Google copy this,

00:40:35.860 --> 00:40:39.940
or Facebook beat this, competition
doesn't factor in at all.

00:40:39.940 --> 00:40:42.690
I definitely don't want
to see your bullshit math,

00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:45.550
